  "notes": "Cash-basis governmental funds, accrual-basis business-type (Water/Sewer enterprise fund; the Statement of Activities p2 business-type column is also accrual and ties: charges 323,454, expenses 513,134). Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Total column of the governmental funds statement (p4). Fund balance 1,154,494 -> 1,362,427 (p4); beginning cash not printed; ending cash = checking accounts 944,361 and certificates of deposit 418,066 (p3). Transfers: Total column prints net (30,547) out (to Water/Sewer, which shows 30,547 in). Pass-through grant in/out 68,583 each (General Fund) netted in other_financing (0). General Fund prints 93,655 for both Intergovernmental and State aid equalization (recorded as printed). Business-type from p6; total expenses 513,134 printed on p2 (operating 486,906 + interest 26,228). Proprietary cash flow statement (p7) left out (proprietary null for cash-basis reports, as FY2024): operating -75,759, capital and related financing -65,681, cash 267,448 to 126,008. Balance sheet: Statement of Financial Position (p1), governmental cash/CD lines from the governmental funds balance sheet Total column (p3; total 1,362,427 = government-wide governmental column p1). Detail: the only governmental supplementary schedule is the combined all-governmental-funds budget schedule (p9), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement (p4); Water/Sewer uses its own cash-basis budget schedule (p10, budget and actual), as FY2024, rather than the accrual statement lines. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
